            description: "(vee-DAHL) (Vidal 256) is a productive white grape that produces excellent quality wine when the fruit reaches reasonable maturity. It requires sites with long growing seasons and moderate winter temperatures. Budbreak is late, which reduces the risk of spring freeze injury. It bears small berries on very large, loose, tapering clusters. Cluster thinning is sometimes required to prevent overcropping. The berries have thick skins, and"
