            description: "(Plant patent 5588) is a fruity, white wine grape derived from Seyval, but its vine is more cold hardy, its fruit ripens slightly earlier, and its wine is somewhat fruitier than Seyval. La Crosse has performed very well in Indiana and is a good choice for the northern half of the state"
